Step 1: Create MVC Project
     1. Open Visual Studio 2026.
     2. Create: ASP.NET Core Web App (Model-View-Controller).
     3. Project Name: AuthDemo
     4. Framework: .NET 10
     5. Click Next.
Step 2: Select Authentication Type
In the Additional Information window:
     •   Choose: Individual Accounts
     •   Click: Create
Visual Studio automatically configures:
     •   Authentication
     •   Authorization
     •   Identity
     •   Login/Register pages
Step 3: Build Project
Go to:
Build → Rebuild Solution
Step 4: Create Database
Open:
Tools → NuGet Package Manager → Package Manager Console
Run:
Update-Database
Identity tables are automatically created.
Step 5: Run Application
Run the application.
Step 6: Register User
      1. Click Register (at the top-right corner of the web application).
      2. Enter:
             o    Email
             o    Password
             o    Confirm Password
      3. Click Register.
User account created successfully.
Step 7: Login
      1. Click Login (at the top-right corner of the web application).
      2. Enter your credentials:
             o    Email
             o    Password
      3. Click Log in.
Step 8: Add Authorized Page
Open HomeController.cs.
At the top, add:
using Microsoft.AspNetCore.Authorization;
Add the following method:
[Authorize]
public IActionResult Secret()
{
     return View();
}
Step 9: Create Secret View
Create the folder only if needed:
Views/Home
Right-click the Home folder → Add → View → Select Razor View – Empty.
View Name: Secret.cshtml
Write the following code in the empty area below the prewritten lines:
<h2>Authorized Users Only</h2>
